<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Text To Word</title></head><body><p>DAY 4 TASK--JAVA TRAINING <br>----------------------------------------------&gt; FOR LOOP <br>1. Print Numbers from 1 to 50 <br><br>public class main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 50; i++) { <br>System.out.println(i); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>2. Print all odd numbers from 1 to 100. <br><br>public class main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 100; i+=2) { <br>System.out.println(i); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>3.Find the sum of numbers from 1 to 100. <br><br>public class main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>int sum = 0; <br><br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 100; i++) { <br>sum = sum + i; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Sum: " + sum); <br>} <br>} <br><br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>4. Print the multiplication table of a number entered by the user. <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 10; i++) { <br>System.out.println(n + " x " + i + " = " + (n * i)); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>5. Find the factorial of a number. <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>long fact = 1; <br><br>if (n &lt; 0) { <br>System.out.println("Factorial is not defined for negative numbers"); <br>} else { <br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= n; i++) { <br>fact = fact * i; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Factorial: " + fact); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>6. Count how many numbers between 1 and 100 are divisible by 7. <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>int count = 0; <br><br>for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 100; i++) { <br>if (i % 7 == 0) { <br>count++; <br>} <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Count: " + count); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>7. Print numbers from 100 down to 1. <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>for (int i = 100; i &gt;= 1; i--) { <br>System.out.println(i); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>8. Calculate the sum of all even numbers from 1 to N. <br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter N: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int sum = 0; <br><br>for (int i = 2; i &lt;= n; i += 2) { <br>sum = sum + i; <br>} <br>System.out.println("Sum: " + sum); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>----------------------------------------------&gt; WHILE LOOP <br><br>1. Print Numbers from 1 to 20 Using While Loop <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>int i = 1; <br><br>while (i &lt;= 20) { <br>System.out.println(i); <br>i++; <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>2. Find the Sum of the Digits of a Number <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int sum = 0; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>int digit = n % 10; <br>sum = sum + digit; <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Sum: " + sum); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>3. Count the Digits in a Positive Integer <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a positive integer: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int count = 0; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>count++; <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Count: " + count); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>4. Reverse a Positive Integer <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int reverse = 0; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>int digit = n % 10; <br>reverse = reverse * 10 + digit; <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Reverse: " + reverse); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>5. Check Whether a Number Is a Palindrome <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int original = n; <br>int reverse = 0; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>int digit = n % 10; <br>reverse = reverse * 10 + digit; <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>if (original == reverse) { <br>System.out.println("Palindrome"); <br>} else { <br>System.out.println("Not a Palindrome"); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>6. Find the Product of the Digits of a Number <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int product = 1; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>int digit = n % 10; <br>product = product * digit; <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>System.out.println("Product: " + product); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>7. Check Whether a Number Is an Armstrong Number <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter a number: "); <br>int n = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>int original = n; <br>int sum = 0; <br><br>while (n &gt; 0) { <br>int digit = n % 10; <br>sum = sum + (digit * digit * digit); <br>n = n / 10; <br>} <br><br>if (original == sum) { <br>System.out.println("Armstrong Number"); <br>} else { <br>System.out.println("Not an Armstrong Number"); <br>} <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>–------------------------------------------&gt; Do-While Loop <br><br>1. Print Numbers from 1 to 10 <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>int i = 1; <br><br>do { <br>System.out.println(i); <br>i++; <br>} while (i &lt;= 10); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br>2. Print a Menu at Least Once <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br>int choice; <br><br>do { <br>System.out.println("1. Add"); <br>System.out.println("2. Subtract"); <br>System.out.println("3. Exit"); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter your choice: "); <br>choice = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>} while (choice != 3); <br><br>System.out.println("Program ended"); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>3. Ask the User to Enter a PIN Until the Correct PIN Is Entered <br><br>import java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>int pin; <br>do { <br>System.out.print("Enter PIN: "); <br>pin = sc.nextInt(); <br>} while (pin != 1234); <br>System.out.println("Correct PIN"); <br>} <br>} <br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br>4. Create a Calculator Menu That Repeats Until the User Chooses Exit <br><br>iimport java.util.Scanner; <br><br>public class Main { <br>public static void main(String[] args) { <br>Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in); <br><br>int choice; <br>int a, b; <br><br>do { <br>System.out.println("\n1. Addition"); <br>System.out.println("2. Subtraction"); <br>System.out.println("3. Multiplication"); <br>System.out.println("4. Division"); <br>System.out.println("5. Exit"); <br><br>System.out.print("Enter your choice: "); <br>choice = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>if (choice &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; choice &lt;= 4) { <br>System.out.print("Enter two numbers: "); <br>a = sc.nextInt(); <br>b = sc.nextInt(); <br><br>if (choice == 1) { <br>System.out.println("Sum: " + (a + b)); <br>} else if (choice == 2) { <br>System.out.println("Difference: " + (a - b)); <br>} else if (choice == 3) { <br>System.out.println("Product: " + (a * b)); <br>} else if (choice == 4) { <br>if (b != 0) { <br>System.out.println("Division: " + ((double) a / b)); <br>} else { <br>System.out.println("Error: Cannot divide by zero."); <br>} <br>} <br><br>} else if (choice != 5) { <br>System.out.println("Invalid choice"); <br>} <br><br>} while (choice != 5); <br><br>System.out.println("Calculator closed"); <br><br>sc.close(); <br>} <br>} <br><br>======================================================================================================================================================================= <br><br></p></body></html>